<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The autoticket module's prompts: the text Metaform sends to agents for the autoticket module.
     Each element is one prompt, named by its tag. What is between the tags is sent exactly as written.
     Comments are never sent.

     Two prompts are read by the code and are not here yet: <intake_step>, sent at connect to an intake agent while
     the module is on and no log is configured, and <connect_notice>, sent at connect to the person's own agent in the
     same state. Their wording is the person's: drafts wait for approval in artifacts/specs-draft/autoticket-prompts.md.
     While an element is absent or empty, nothing is sent. -->
<prompts>
<!-- autoticket's line in the connect message, after the module's name. Empty, as here, sends nothing. Off until the
     module is enabled. -->
<connect></connect>
<!-- autoticket's instructions. Returned by metaform_instructions with module autoticket, at
     metaform://instructions/autoticket, and printed by metaform help agents autoticket. Off until the module is
     enabled. -->
<instructions>autoticket is active.</instructions>
<!-- The line under the counts an agent is told at its node. autoticket counts nothing at nodes, so it is empty. -->
<counts></counts>
<!-- autoticket's rules, MCP-031. Empty sends nothing. -->
<rules></rules>
<!-- The task of a ticket autoticket files for a new kind of error, read by the agent that takes it, under Autostart
     the one dispatch starts. The empty elements are filled in: message, the error's first line; source, what raised
     it (the web server, the web page, an MCP tool call, an agent run, a feedback report or a watched log); count,
     first and last, how often and when it was seen when filed; sample, its example with secrets masked; reproduce,
     how its source says to make it happen again. Later counts go to the ticket's note. Wording drafted for the
     person's approval, ticket code.scheduler.task#8 (2026-10-18). -->
<ticket>An error was seen while the project ran, and nothing has fixed it yet. Find its cause and fix it.

What failed: <message/>
Raised by <source/>, seen <count/>, first <first/>, last <last/>.
A sample, with secrets masked:
<sample/>

How to reproduce it: <reproduce/>

The fix comes with a check that proves this error no longer happens: a test that fails before the fix and passes after it, or the reproduction above run again without the error. Say in your resolution what the check was and what it showed. The ticket's note counts each time the error comes back while the ticket is open.

If the fix is a design choice, or would delete or remove data, do not make it: write what you found and the choice in this ticket's note, and stop with the ticket open, for the person to decide.</ticket>
<!-- Why a ticket filed for a feedback report waits for the person, in Backlog: written at the start of its note. -->
<held_design>Feedback says how Metaform should work, and what to change is a design choice.</held_design>
<!-- Why a ticket filed for an error naming deleting or removing data waits for the person, in Backlog: written at the
     start of its note. -->
<held_data>The error is about deleting or removing data, so its fix may delete or remove data.</held_data>
</prompts>
